{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1179124-heads-of-the-hydra","id":1179124,"title":"Heads of the Hydra","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-01-24T23:19:45-08:00","id":1179124,"title":"Heads of the Hydra","content":"I was a little unclear on the different Books of the Wyrm usage of the phrase &quot;physically manifest&quot; if it just meant manifesting in the world of the flesh, or if it meant appearing in a cohesive form in the Umbra.<br /> <br /> Are the Triatic Wyrm something that can be observed and interacted with directly in Malfeas? Or is their appearance in any form, even in the Umbra, reserved for the Apocalypse &amp; near misses (if defeated), such as the fall of Roanoke. Similarly, to what degree are the Urge Wyrms entities whose existence matters at all? Are they just a metaphysical flavor detail on the Maeljin Incarnae, or do they also exist in a form that can actually be interacted with in some way?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T09:17:39-08:00","id":1179225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1179124-heads-of-the-hydra#post1179124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was a little unclear on the different Books of the Wyrm usage of the phrase &quot;physically manifest&quot; if it just meant manifesting in the world of the flesh, or if it meant appearing in a cohesive form in the Umbra.<br /> <br /> Are the Triatic Wyrm something that can be observed and interacted with directly in Malfeas? Or is their appearance in any form, even in the Umbra, reserved for the Apocalypse &amp; near misses (if defeated), such as the fall of Roanoke. Similarly, to what degree are the Urge Wyrms entities whose existence matters at all? Are they just a metaphysical flavor detail on the Maeljin Incarnae, or do they also exist in a form that can actually be interacted with in some way?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Triatic Wyrms are Celestines, so you can't really safely observe or communicate with them anywhere, least of all Malfeas. The Urge Wyrms are the worries of the Wyrm that are smaller than trying to figure out where things went wrong, and they basically make the existence of Maeljin possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T19:07:24-08:00","id":1179392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1179124-heads-of-the-hydra?p=1179225#post1179225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">so you can't really safely observe or communicate with them anywhere, least of all Malfeas</div> </div> </div> </div>I know not safely. I'm just wondering if they're &quot;there&quot; in Malfeas towering over the Duchies. If outside of their potential manifestation at the Battlefield of the Apocalypse, they can be perceived in any form anywhere at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T22:06:17-08:00","id":1181013,"title":"","content":"Ok, my understanding looking over previous editions Books of the Wyrm and Umbra books - Malfeas is a Near Umbra Realm, and thus Incarnae are the highest rank spirits that will normally manifest there (outside of an Apocalyptic event). At its heart, the lowest depths of the Black Spiral, is an Anchorhead that leads to the direct presence of the Triatic Wyrm Celestines in the Deep Umbra. Effectively Malfeas is a cyst that formed around said Anchorhead.<br /> <br /> Does that seem accurate?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T13:04:55-08:00","id":1181203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1179124-heads-of-the-hydra?p=1181013#post1181013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, my understanding looking over previous editions Books of the Wyrm and Umbra books - Malfeas is a Near Umbra Realm, and thus Incarnae are the highest rank spirits that will normally manifest there (outside of an Apocalyptic event). At its heart, the lowest depths of the Black Spiral, is an Anchorhead that leads to the direct presence of the Triatic Wyrm Celestines in the Deep Umbra. Effectively Malfeas is a cyst that formed around said Anchorhead.<br /> <br /> Does that seem accurate?</div> </div> </div> </div>The passages in 2e and Revised put together a slightly different picture, where the whole of Malfeas used to be in the Deep Umbra (said to be the home of the Triat) but moved closer to the material Gaia Realm as the Apocalypse loomed on the horizon. A midway between those two states wasn't mentioned in the books, but it's far from out of the question for it to look like that in a game where the clock is ticking, as a kind of &quot;two minutes to midnight&quot; type of setup.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}